                <pb facs="0264" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg158"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Hicks.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-04">September 4,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Adee informs Mr. Hicks that he is named special representative of the
                    American National Red Cross to receive funds raised here for the earthquake
                    sufferers, and is to distribute them through the Red Cross of Chile, or as he
                    thinks best. Mr. Hicks is also told to notify the Chilean Government and consult
                    it as to the disposition of the funds.</p>
            </div>
